812,"e":40836,"k":"block","t":"Terminal-only fullscreen","f":[]},{"s":40845,"e":41658,"k":"block","t":"Press KTPH006KTPH000KTPH007+KTPH008KTPH001KTPH009+KTPH010KTPH002KTPH011 (or KTPH012View → Terminal-only FullscreenKTPH013) to show the whole korTTY window — menus, tabs and status bar included — kept at its previous window size and centered on an empty fullscreen background, so the desktop and other windows stop competing for attention. KTPH014View → Hide terminal scrollbars in fullscreenKTPH015 removes the scrollbars too. A transparent terminal background becomes opaque while fullscreen is active and returns to its saved level when you leave. Press KTPH016KTPH003KTPH017+KTPH018KTPH004KTPH019+KTPH020KTPH005KTPH021 again to restore.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-f\">F</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-f\">F</kbd>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>"]},{"s":41691,"e":41773,"k":"block","t":"DashboardKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#dashboard\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":41783,"e":42109,"k":"block","t":"Toggle the dashboard with KTPH003KTPH000KTPH004+KTPH005KTPH001KTPH006+KTPH007KTPH002KTPH008 or KTPH009View → Show DashboardKTPH010. It slides in on the left, sizes its width to the longest entry, and follows the active App Design's colors.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-d\">D</kbd>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":42118,"e":42338,"k":"block","t":"The header shows the panel title with two buttons: a collapse/expand toggle (collapses everything while any node is open, expands everything otherwise) and a refresh button. Below it, connections are organized as a tree:","f":[]},{"s":42354,"e":42435,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Main windowKTPH001 — the root node, with an active/total session count.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":42446,"e":42684,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000EnvironmentsKTPH001 — connections whose stored credential has an environment (for example KTPH002ProductionKTPH003 or KTPH004TestKTPH005) are clustered under an environment node; connections without one sit directly under the main window.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<em>","</em>","<em>","</em>"]},{"s":42695,"e":42867,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000GroupsKTPH001 — tabs assigned to a connection group appear under their group node. Saving a changed group in the Connection Manager updates open tabs immediately.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":42884,"e":43516,"k":"block","t":"Each connection row shows a type icon, a status dot, the server name, and a protocol badge (KTPH000, KTPH001 or KTPH002). The status dot distinguishes three states: filled green for a healthy connection, filled red for a connection that dropped unexpectedly (including a Mosh network interruption), and a hollow outline for a session that ended normally. Terminals with AI-agent runs carry the same ✋/⚡/⏸/✓ badge as elsewhere. Hovering a row shows KTPH003 and the connection state; double-click (or KTPH005KTPH004KTPH006) focuses the session's tab.","f":["<code>ssh</code>","<code>mosh</code>","<code>local</code>","<code>user@host</code>","<kbd class=\"key-enter\">Enter</kbd>","<span class=\"keys\">","</span>"]},{"s":43525,"e":43842,"k":"block","t":"Right-click a connection for KTPH000FocusKTPH001, KTPH002DuplicateKTPH003, KTPH004ReconnectKTPH005, KTPH006SFTP-Client...KTPH007 (connected sessions only) and KTPH008CloseKTPH009. A footer keeps a running \"connected of total\" count, and an empty panel shows a placeholder until the first session opens.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":43873,"e":43967,"k":"block","t":"macOS Dock menuKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#macos-dock-menu\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":43977,"e":44173,"k":"block","t":"On macOS, right-click (or Control-click) the korTTY icon in the Dock for quick actions without switching to the app — they apply to the current (focused) window, opening one first if none is open:","f":[]},{"s":44189,"e":44216,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000New WindowKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":44227,"e":44269,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000New Tab in Current WindowKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":44280,"e":44337,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Manage Connections…KTPH001 (Connection Manager)","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":44348,"e":44378,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Open Project…KTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":44389,"e":44431,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000ManualKTPH001 (the in-app guide)","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":44442,"e":44471,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000About korTTYKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":44488,"e":44690,"k":"block","t":"See the KTPH000menu referenceKTPH001 for every menu item and the KTPH002keyboard-shortcuts referenceKTPH003 for the full list of accelerators.","f":["<a href=\"../reference/menu.html\">","</a>","<a href=\"../reference/keyboard-shortcuts.html\">","</a>"]},{"s":45586,"e":45603,"k":"text","t":"\r\n  Back to top\r\n","f":[]},{"s":45858,"e":45899,"k":"text","t":"MIT-licensed · Developed by Daniel Mengel","f":[]},{"s":45946,"e":45959,"k":"text","t":"\r\n    korTTY ","f":[]},{"s":45967,"e":45974,"k":"text","t":"v2.14.0","f":[]}]}